From 5ed0115f9459f5de8c8522c7b46dfa6a5d40ae6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 13:29:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0119 -- SB16 WaveBlaster music volume (CT1745
 Line-In + CD)

Task #7 (A4) SDL side. Exposes a user-facing WaveBlaster/wavetable music volume
control that the existing SETUP "Music volume" cannot reach.

Why DOS needs this: SETUP's "Music volume" maps to SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SB16_FM_VOL,
which programs only the CT1745 FM register (0x34/0x35 = OPL3 FM music). A
WaveBlaster/DreamBlaster daughterboard on the SB16 header is a SEPARATE MIDI
device whose ANALOG output is summed into the SB16 mixer via a different input --
Line-In (0x38/0x39) or CD (0x36/0x37), NOT the OPL3 FM path -- so the FM slider
does nothing for WB music, and WB users have no volume control (operator note:
WB music quieter than OPL3). Which input the header feeds is HW-uncertain across
cards; the existing SDL/0100 LINEIN_VOL/CD_VOL knobs A/B-pin it on g2k.

New hint SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_WB_MUSIC_VOL (0..31, CT1745 5-bit level<<3) programs
BOTH candidate inputs to the requested level: the input the WB does not use
carries no signal on the WB config, so programming it too is harmless, and one
SETUP slider then works regardless of which input is live -- no shipped register
guess. DEFAULT UNSET = mixer untouched = byte-identical to SDL/0100 (killswitch
by absence). Applied BEFORE the individual LINEIN_VOL/CD_VOL knobs so an A/B
setting one of those still overrides + isolates the live input for the docs.
Scoped to is_sb16 + the same SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SB16_MIXER_PROGRAM killswitch as
the rest of the CT1745 balance block. Banner: "audio: SDL/0119 SB16 WaveBlaster
music vol=N (...)".

Config key WB_MUSIC_VOL -> env SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_WB_MUSIC_VOL, surfaced by SETUP
(coordinated with setup-eng). g2k: A/B a few levels (and LINEIN-only vs CD-only
via the SDL/0100 knobs) to confirm WB responds + pin the live input for docs.

Workspace-local patch; not upstreamed (sdl_ai_policy).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index 00e091b9f..dec93dfcc 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -3010,6 +3010,37 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
                    to is_sb16 + the same SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SB16_MIXER_PROGRAM
                    killswitch as the rest of this block. */
                 {
+                    /* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0119, task #7): user-facing WaveBlaster
+                       music volume. SETUP's "Music volume" only drives OPL3 FM
+                       (SB16_FM_VOL / 0x34-0x35 above), so it does NOT affect
+                       WaveBlaster/DreamBlaster MIDI music -- the WB daughterboard's
+                       analog output is summed into the SB16 mixer via Line-In
+                       (0x38/0x39) or CD (0x36/0x37), NOT the OPL3 FM path. Which of
+                       the two the header feeds is HW-uncertain (the SDL/0100 knobs
+                       below A/B-pin it on g2k), so this single SETUP-facing knob
+                       programs BOTH candidate inputs to `wv`: the input the WB does
+                       NOT use carries no signal on the WB config, so programming it
+                       too is harmless and the slider works regardless of which one
+                       is live -- no shipped register guess. Value 0..31 (CT1745
+                       5-bit level<<3, like the rest of this block). DEFAULT UNSET =
+                       not programmed = byte-identical to SDL/0100 (killswitch by
+                       absence). Applied BEFORE the individual LINEIN_VOL/CD_VOL
+                       knobs below so an A/B setting one of those still OVERRIDES
+                       this and isolates the live input for the docs. Config key
+                       WB_MUSIC_VOL -> env SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_WB_MUSIC_VOL (SETUP /
+                       nx-engine, task A4). Scoped to is_sb16 + the same
+                       SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SB16_MIXER_PROGRAM killswitch. */
+                    const char *wb = SDL_GetHint("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_WB_MUSIC_VOL");
+                    if (wb && wb[0] != '\0') {
+                        int wv = SDL_atoi(wb); wv = (wv < 0) ? 0 : (wv > 31) ? 31 : wv;
+                        outportb(mixer_addr, 0x38); outportb(mixer_data, (Uint8)(wv << 3)); // Line-In L
+                        outportb(mixer_addr, 0x39); outportb(mixer_data, (Uint8)(wv << 3)); // Line-In R
+                        outportb(mixer_addr, 0x36); outportb(mixer_data, (Uint8)(wv << 3)); // CD L
+                        outportb(mixer_addr, 0x37); outportb(mixer_data, (Uint8)(wv << 3)); // CD R
+                        doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0119 SB16 WaveBlaster music vol=%d "
+                                         "(CT1745 Line-In 0x38/0x39 + CD 0x36/0x37; both "
+                                         "WB-candidate inputs; SETUP WB_MUSIC_VOL)", wv);
+                    }
                     const char *li = SDL_GetHint("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SB16_LINEIN_VOL");
                     const char *cd = SDL_GetHint("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SB16_CD_VOL");
                     if (li && li[0] != '\0') {
